WEBVTT

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:03.890
You're pretty, positive, 
and you never lose heart.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.400
You have friends, and even a boyfriend.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.640
And you want to be Queen, too?

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.230
You can't.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.460
Please play me next, Master!

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.870
Sudo-kun, did you lose?

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:29.490
I won! Two to nothing!

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.040
<i>But just barely, damn it.</i>

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:34.580
No. I have no reason to.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.170
In fact, I hate you.

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:41.850
<i>He's gonna go places!
He knows how to climb the ladder!</i>

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:44.310
<b>For you</b>

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.300
<i>You don't see many high school 
second-years with that knack!</i>

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:52.440
<b>Super persistent type</b>

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:52.440
<b>The type that never learns</b>

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:52.440
Ayase, would you rather play me
or Koishikawa-san now?

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:56.930
Ishida-san, play a match with her.

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:57.860
Okay.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:07.080
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.910
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.940
Verse 16

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.940
Takes me 
away in 
haste

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:19.740
Why did you say that to Chihaya?

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:22.990
You can't.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:27.250
When I see someone as straight as 
an arrow, I want to bend them.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.780
Don't verbally bend someone who didn't 
bend to you during your match!

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:39.120
I'm going to start now.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:46.920
<i>Naniwa Bay, now the flower 
blooms, but for winter</i>

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:51.050
Thank you very much.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:54.840
<i>I lost! I lost again... again...</i>

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:57.230
<b>Class B</b>

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.330
Thank you very much.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:02.150
<i>Suo-san won by 14 cards.</i>

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:04.200
<i>That was his target number.</i>

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:04.200
<b>He's as nasty as ever</b>

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:07.950
<i>But that kid didn't commit
a single fault against him.</i>

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.820
<i>How long has it been since that happened?</i>

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:14.440
<i>Suo-san was made to take 25 cards the legit way.</i>

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.050
Thanks a lot. We appreciate your help.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:22.010
You two really are good.

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:23.420
This was fun! We should—

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.000
Give Dr. Harada my regards.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:27.440
And...

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:29.750
Don't come again.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:40.690
Crap, sorry.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:42.400
I forgot something.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:45.340
I'll be a while,
 so go ahead and grab a train.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:46.690
Oh, okay.

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:47.810
And be careful!

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:58.690
Bye!

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:01.720
I don't even need dinner.
I had too much red bean soup.

00:03:58.690 --> 00:03:59.870
See ya.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.340
Suo-san!

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.180
Can we do a review of our match?

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:12.000
A review?

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.330
Like when go and shogi players
analyze a match in depth by re-enacting it?

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.990
Not many karuta players do that, right?

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:20.620
No. I have no reason to.

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:22.810
In fact, I hate you.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.350
Go home with your girlfriend.

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:28.180
She's not actually my girlfriend.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:30.490
I was bluffing. I'm sorry.

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:33.080
Grab.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.580
<i>He's gonna go places...</i>

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.580
<b>He's gonna go places...</b>

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:42.170
<i>Ow...</i>

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:46.090
<i>His music's so loud, I can hear it 
in the middle of a packed train.</i>

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:49.330
<i>I'll never use earbuds.</i>

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:52.480
<i>And if I ever need headphones,
 I'll keep them at the minimum volume.</i>

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.150
<i>My ears are my life.</i>

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:58.540
You're pretty, positive, 
and you never lose heart.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:00.710
You have friends, and even a boyfriend.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:02.540
And you want to be Queen, too?

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.320
You can't.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:06.870
<i>What boyfriend?</i>

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:08.100
<i>You can't.</i>

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:10.330
You can't.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:16.130
<i>The Master...</i>

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.390
<i>His game sense is extraordinary.</i>

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:21.990
<i>He's a genius.</i>

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:29.440
Chihaya-chan? What brings 
you here at this hour?

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:32.830
Dr. Harada, I think I figured it out!

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:36.140
Suo-san's weakness!

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:57.160
Did you really feel that?

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:02.070
But is that a weakness? 
Considering it's Suo-kun...

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:04.350
it could also be a strength.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:07.770
I'll take you home.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:13.800
I'm surprised Suo-kun played a 
practice match with you, though.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.350
What's the world coming to?

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.930
I hear he's been hanging 
around Queen Wakamiya, too.

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:20.180
You'd better stay alert.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.220
And you want to be Queen, too?

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.230
Chihaya-chan.

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:31.290
Don't tell anyone what 
you just told me, okay?

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:33.700
You don't think it would be helpful?

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.570
For the time being...

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:38.300
I want to make sure it only helps me!

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:42.080
Goodnight, Dr. Harada!

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:51.310
You can't.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:56.270
Tsusaki Private
High School

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.980
Let's see... Wakamiya-san.

00:06:56.980 --> 00:07:00.690
For now, you plan to move on
to Tsusaki University,

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:03.560
and for now, you'll be 
studying the humanities.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:07.600
Well, I'm sure you won't be 
the Queen of karuta forever.

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:10.560
It wouldn't hurt to think about 
what sort of career you'd like...

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:15.450
Interview Notes

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:15.450
But you come from a respectable family, 
so I'm sure there's no need to worry.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.800
Oh, Wakamiya-san, you had your 
interview today, right?

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:20.700
The teacher isn't putting much 
thought into these, is she?

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.940
She just thinks we're all little rich girls.

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:27.180
But you've got it good, Wakamiya-san. 
You're the Queen of karuta!

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:30.290
I heard they're not broadcasting 
this year's match on TV.

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:32.280
Too bad. Not that I ever watched it.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:34.640
I don't know much about it, 
but I'll be rooting for you!

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:39.910
<i>I couldn't enter any fall tournaments 
because I always had a cold.</i>

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:42.640
<i>I haven't had enough practice 
in actual matches.</i>

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:47.440
<i>The challenger in the Queen match 
is Inokuma Haruka, grade 6,</i>

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:50.100
<i>a former Queen who defended 
her title several times.</i>

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:51.900
<i>I met her once.</i>

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:54.780
<i>The air she had about her wasn't normal.</i>

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:57.730
<i>It was so easy to make the 
assumption that she was good.</i>

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.080
<b>Grr</b>

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:06.270
<i>I haven't been up to par since 
I lost to Arata in the summer.</i>

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:09.510
<i>And then Arata went on to lose 
in the challenger playoff...</i>

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:10.090
<b>That smiling four-eyes is pathetic</b>

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:17.600
<b>Snowhime is here!!</b>

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:16.700
<i>Fujioka's kimono shop has 
Japanese-style Snowmaru goods!</i>

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:17.600
<i>I want!</i>

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:19.860
<i>Money pouches! Folding fans! Sachets!</i>

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:26.610
<b>Snownokomachi</b>

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:22.610
Only two Snowmaru purchases per month!

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:25.210
You've gotta stop buying 
all these silly things!

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.610
You're not even making your own money!

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:30.990
<b>Mom doesn't 
make that 
much money, 
either</b>

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:31.990
<i>Well, if I lose the Queen match,</i>

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:33.610
<i>I'll have nothing left.</i>

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.710
<i>Oh, come on...</i>

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:44.770
<i>She's been doing so well over the fall,
and now she's in a slump?</i>

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:46.920
<i>She's not concentrating.</i>

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.950
It's about to get dark, 
so let's call it a day.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:51.530
Start cleaning up.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.840
<b><i>Competitive
Karuta Club
New members always welcome!</i></b>

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:56.800
Chihaya-chan, are you heading 
to the Shiranami Society now?

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:59.520
Yeah, to play some matches with Dr. Harada.

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:01.920
Are you doing the same, President Mashima?

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:04.310
Huh? Uh, no...

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:05.800
I'm...

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:11.720
Hey, Taichi...

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:14.320
How did playing against 
Suo-san feel to you?

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.680
Huh? I guess it felt...

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:20.340
like a struggle.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:25.850
<i>In the seven minutes we spent 
walking to the station...</i>

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:30.790
There are only four outcomes in karuta, right?

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:33.050
<i>The four outcomes...</i>

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:36.720
<i>You take cards, your opponent takes cards,</i>

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:41.070
<i>you make mistakes, or your 
opponent makes mistakes.</i>

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:44.060
<i>Dr. Harada uses some tricky techniques,</i>

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:47.890
<i>but his offensive karuta means his style
 is to be the one taking cards.</i>

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:50.330
<i>That's the same for most players.</i>

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:53.570
<i>Chihaya and Arata, too.</i>

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:58.310
You had zero faults today.

00:09:59.090 --> 00:09:59.940
You...

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:02.360
give me a bad feeling.

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:07.340
<i>Making your opponent mess up...</i>

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:10.770
<i>There's a style which focuses on that alone,</i>

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:14.260
<i>and there's a part of me that finds it appealing.</i>

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:18.620
People!

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:22.930
Karuta is important, but there's more 
important stuff we need to think about now!

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:27.430
December 24th 
Tsukuba 
Household

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:30.100
Sorry, there's not very much space.

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.650
There's lots of space!
And there are lots of people!

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.570
<i>Tsukuba's mom is gorgeous!</i>

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:38.610
Hey, little brothers! Let's eat!

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:39.700
Come on down!

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:40.890
No!

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:43.240
This year, we're waiting up here
until Santa comes!

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:46.200
We're not going to sleep until
he gives us our presents in person!

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:49.330
The three little brothers 
are in their room.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:50.780
Just as planned.

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:51.830
Roger.

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:55.840
<b>*MCS... Mizusawa Claus Squad</b>

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:55.850
MCS Team A, follow the script...

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:57.220
and climb up!

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:01.210
Do you think he'll come?

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:02.370
I know he will.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.800
But the ogre was totally Dad.

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:06.530
If Santa doesn't come...

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:12.480
Merry Chri—

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:17.770
Someone's here!

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:18.700
It's Santa!

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:19.920
I'm scared!

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:21.360
What? Santa's here?

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:22.890
That's wonderful!

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:24.540
Why did you run away?

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:25.620
Huh?

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:27.380
Go on, get back in there.

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:29.250
He might have something for you.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:30.660
O-Okay...

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:31.540
Go on.

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:40.930
A tiny music player...

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:42.770
A CD of Igarashi-san's reading...

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:44.890
New karuta cards...

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:48.770
Thanks, Santa-san!

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:51.300
Sorry we ran away! Come on back!

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:52.650
There's one for you too, bro!

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:57.570
<b>To Akihiro-kun,
 who loves 
his brothers 
From Santa</b>

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:57.610
<b>Protect Your Knees 
Supporter DX</b>

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.530
<b>To Akihiro-kun,
 who loves 
his brothers 
From Santa</b>

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:01.360
This is awesome, guys!

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:04.850
If we put Igarashi-san's reading 
on this player and randomize it,

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:07.040
we won't have to take 
turns reading anymore!

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:10.120
We can practice two-on-two at home!

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:13.040
We're gonna get so much better!

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:14.540
We'll see him next year for sure!

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:15.710
Next year, too?!

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.230
You were eating chicken!

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:18.860
I want chicken, too!

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:20.800
I'm hungry!

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:22.920
<i>Thank you, Santa-san.</i>

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:28.920
You okay, Ayase? We 
actually pulled it of—

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:33.230
<b>Sob 
Sob 
Sob 
Sob 
Sob 
Sob 
Sob</b>

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:37.370
Stop crying, Ayase.

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:38.730
But...

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:41.540
The makeup tricks my sister 
used to make me look fat

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:45.240
<b>MCS Script</b>

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:45.240
<b>I put in blue colored
 contacts and even 
used white mascara 
on my eyelashes...</b>

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:45.240
and the script you wrote that I actually 
memorized were made useless in one second!

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:48.310
No, that actually went great.

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:50.680
If Porky had done it,
they would've known instantly.

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:53.670
You were the one least likely to dress 
as Santa, which is why it worked.

00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:56.800
I actually memorized all of Santa's lines!

00:12:56.800 --> 00:13:00.190
Y'know, since you have such sharp hearing, 
your pronunciation sounded almost native!

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:02.160
You don't feel disappointed at all?!

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:05.100
You wrote out the entire scene, 
right up to the tearful goodbye!

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:06.640
The Heisei literary master...

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:06.630
Uh, yeah, I guess...

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:08.500
But...

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:11.360
They were really happy.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:16.010
And Tsukuba's little brothers are 
basically our little brothers.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:21.070
Anyway, you look scary,
so could you lose the makeup now?

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:21.730
Oh... Yeah.

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:24.740
<b>She even stuffed her nostrils?!</b>

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:28.730
Ayase, you know...

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:32.650
At Christmas last year, we all had 
our own class parties, right?

00:13:32.650 --> 00:13:34.740
That was fun too,

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:37.990
but since I didn't have many friends, 
I realize even more now...

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:39.750
that for me,

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:42.510
spending it with everyone is like a dream.

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:47.960
They say the people you 
wish were there with you

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:51.440
are your family.

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:54.220
How long you've known each other
and how close you are don't matter.

00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:58.560
Ayase, look!

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:00.460
Tsukuba's mom is amazing!

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:02.660
I thought this was gelatin, 
but it's agar jelly noodles!

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:03.310
Guys...

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:06.200
Who wants to go see
the Master and Queen matches?

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:08.980
H-Huh?

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:10.310
If we can be back the same day.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:15.080
Sure! Let's save our New Year's money 
so we can make it a day trip!

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:17.210
<i>Arata...</i>

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:19.590
<i>Arata...</i>

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:22.320
<i>Arata...</i>

00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:27.320
<i>I'm a bit off.</i>

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:27.960
<i>Be more...</i>

00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:29.840
<i>more precise!</i>

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:35.090
Shinobu-san is even 
practicing on Christmas?

00:14:35.090 --> 00:14:36.920
Don't say anything to her.

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:39.850
And don't serve cake after 
dinner or anything.

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:42.340
It'll just make her feel even sadder.

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:44.260
Yes, of course.

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:47.110
<i>I'm not sad, though.</i>

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:51.460
<i>I don't know why, but Mom doesn't 
really feel like family to me.</i>

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:56.810
<i>Yeah, it looks best when the princesses 
on platforms are side by side.</i>

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:58.460
<i>Gotta be careful when I take them.</i>

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:02.950
<i>When I practice aiming for corners, 
I can go a lot harder on the monks.</i>

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:07.540
<i>The karuta cards feel a lot more 
like family to me.</i>

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:10.690
<i>The cards are my only family.</i>

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:17.540
Welcome home.

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:22.220
You've been doing this for 
a long time now. Why?

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:25.080
I'm sorry. I'll clean up right away.

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:26.520
It's all right.

00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:28.860
It's nearly time to replace 
the tatami mats, anyway.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:30.360
Thank you.

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:36.900
What I'm doing is...

00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:39.890
I need to be able to take 
cards from anywhere,

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:41.790
but this is practice for taking cards

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:46.410
that are the farthest away on the playing field
 by covering the shortest possible distance.

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:49.090
I've had trouble with that lately.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:51.720
Sh-Shinobu!

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.900
You're playing karuta in the reception 
room again! I told you not to!

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.850
<b>Bit late for that</b>

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:56.630
Do that in your own room!

00:15:56.630 --> 00:15:57.840
I don't like playing on carpet.

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:59.590
That doesn't mean you can't!

00:15:59.590 --> 00:16:01.590
The shortest possible distance?

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:04.970
You mean this?

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:12.350
I've already ordered your kimono for
 the next match from Hidakaya-san.

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:14.480
Oh...

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:18.490
We received dried persimmons from 
Yamanashi. Shall we have some?

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.750
<b>Dried persimmons on Christmas?</b>

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:21.510
I-I'll have some.

00:16:21.510 --> 00:16:23.840
Also, that hairdo looks quite strange.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:29.000
Such refined taste...

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:32.510
January 10th

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:32.510
Shiga Prefecture:
Omi Jingu

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:32.500
I'm so tired!

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:34.510
Even the earliest train 
barely got here in time!

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:37.710
Dr. Harada's staying at the 
Lake Biwa Hotel, right?

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:38.520
He's lucky!

00:16:38.950 --> 00:16:40.880
Be the challenger,
and you can stay there too!

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:45.150
The players are about to 
do their pre-game prayer!

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:50.210
His hair's gotten longer!

00:16:50.210 --> 00:16:51.150
The facial hair, too!

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:56.780
She's thin this year!

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:57.920
And her hair's weird!

00:16:57.920 --> 00:17:00.910
Why is she wearing long sleeves with 
hand-painted Yuzen silk to play karuta?!

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:11.090
<b>57th Queen Match</b>

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:11.090
<b>Ogura Hundred Poets Karuta 
Master and Queen Matches</b>

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:11.100
I got us seats! Really good ones!

00:17:11.100 --> 00:17:12.250
This way!

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:13.660
We can't!

00:17:13.660 --> 00:17:15.680
We're young and inexperienced,

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:17.840
so we should watch it on
the TV in the first floor hall.

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:18.480
Huh?!

00:17:19.610 --> 00:17:21.620
Oh... You can stay, Chihaya-chan.

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:23.820
You're representing the Shiranami cheer squad.

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:26.080
Th-Thank goodness...

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:27.880
I brought my best outfit today.

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:29.180
Your best outfit?

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:34.440
A handkerchief autographed by Daddy Bear,
 for when Dr. Harada wins!

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:36.270
A-Autographed?

00:17:36.270 --> 00:17:39.350
He had a signing event! Only the 
first 50 people to apply got in!

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:40.890
Don't say anything, Kana-chan.

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:42.690
That's a bog too deep to wade into.

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:51.840
<b>57th Queen Match</b>

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:51.840
<b>Ogura Hundred Poets Karuta 
Master and Queen Matches</b>

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:51.840
<b>59th Master Match</b>

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:47.240
It's a bit different from the way 
it looked on TV last year, though.

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:50.110
Yeah, since there's no 
TV broadcast this year,

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:51.830
they apparently changed the setup.

00:17:52.030 --> 00:17:55.770
How could they stop the live broadcast 
of the biggest event in karuta?!

00:17:55.770 --> 00:17:57.350
Is karuta on the decline?!

00:17:57.350 --> 00:17:59.960
It can't decline! It can't decline!

00:17:58.630 --> 00:17:59.960
Tsukuba, be quiet.

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:02.480
I don't think that's why.

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:05.890
It's not just the Master and Queen matches.

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:08.960
A lot of the other major tournaments 
have been streamed online lately,

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:10.230
<b><i>Competitive Karuta 
59th Master Match 
57th Queen Match 
</i></b>The event will begin soon. Please wait.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:10.230
Starting yet?           I'm naked and ready                Can't wait                     Good morning

